# k.diagrams: what each kind of diagram is (block "04:40"): its structure (the structures of k.kinds: graph, sequence,
# whole with parts, cycle, values by category), its layout and the arrangement of k.layouts it uses, the shape each kind
# of node is usually drawn with (a flowchart's decision is a diamond), and which knowledge of the catalog fills it (the
# parts of a thing make a tree, the stages of a cycle a cycle diagram, the steps of a method a flowchart). A host
# draws a diagram of a topic by choosing a kind whose fill the topic has, and makes it in the world schema w.diagram.
# sources: hand-core 1 (the schema and the facts, hand-written in this repository; the works cited are k.diagrams.source facts)
# license: CC0-1.0
# script: none (hand-written); the shards are written by tools/diagrams-core.mjs

@k.diagrams core.module name=k.diagrams version=3 exports=kind exports=shape exports=fill exports=source exports=topic core.source="hand-core 1"

# A published work a fact rests on: `name` a short id (author and year: venn1880), `cite` the reference, `year`.
@k.diagrams.source core.type of=k.diagrams.source shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.source.name core.slot of=k.diagrams.source key=name id=true required=true kind=atom core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.source.cite core.slot of=k.diagrams.source key=cite required=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.source.year core.slot of=k.diagrams.source key=year required=true kind=integer core.source="hand-core 1"

# A kind of diagram. `name` (flowchart, tree, Venn diagram ...); `form` its value of w.diagram.diagram.form; `about` what
# it shows; `structure` the structures of k.kinds it is (many); `layout` how it is laid out (the values of
# w.diagram.diagram.layout: top_down, left_right, radial, circular, grid, overlapping, free); `arranged` the
# arrangements of k.layouts its nodes follow (tree, flow, ring, radial, row, grid ...); `edges` directed (arrows),
# undirected (lines) or none; `role` the roles its nodes play (values of w.diagram.node.role); `usual_for` what it is
# used for; `source` the works it rests on (k.diagrams.source names).
@k.diagrams.kind core.type of=k.diagrams.kind shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.name core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=name id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.form core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=form required=true enum=flowchart enum=tree enum=cycle enum=timeline enum=mind_map enum=venn enum=org_chart enum=network enum=pipeline enum=table core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.about core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=about required=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.structure core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=structure many=true required=true kind=atom kind=string type=k.kinds.structure by=name core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.layout core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=layout many=true required=true enum=top_down enum=left_right enum=radial enum=circular enum=grid enum=overlapping enum=free core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.arranged core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=arranged many=true kind=atom kind=string type=k.layouts.layout by=name core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.edges core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=edges required=true enum=directed enum=undirected enum=none core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.role core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=role many=true required=true enum=start enum=end enum=process enum=decision enum=data enum=document enum=subprocess enum=connector enum=root enum=item enum=stage enum=event enum=centre enum=branch enum=post enum=node enum=row enum=column enum=cell enum=database enum=actor enum=note enum=external core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.groups core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=groups enum=yes enum=no core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.usual_for core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=usual_for many=true required=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.kind.source core.slot of=k.diagrams.kind key=source many=true kind=atom type=k.diagrams.source by=name core.source="hand-core 1"

# The shape a node of a role is usually drawn with in a kind of diagram (`kind` a k.diagrams.kind name, `role`, `shape`
# a value of w.diagram.node.shape, `about`, `source`).
@k.diagrams.shape core.type of=k.diagrams.shape shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.shape.kind core.slot of=k.diagrams.shape key=kind id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string type=k.diagrams.kind by=name core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.shape.role core.slot of=k.diagrams.shape key=role id=true required=true enum=start enum=end enum=process enum=decision enum=data enum=document enum=subprocess enum=connector enum=root enum=item enum=stage enum=event enum=centre enum=branch enum=post enum=node enum=row enum=column enum=cell enum=database enum=actor enum=note enum=external core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.shape.shape core.slot of=k.diagrams.shape key=shape required=true enum=oval enum=rectangle enum=rounded_rectangle enum=diamond enum=parallelogram enum=document enum=double_rectangle enum=circle enum=ellipse enum=dot enum=chevron enum=cylinder enum=cloud enum=actor enum=note core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.shape.about core.slot of=k.diagrams.shape key=about required=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.shape.source core.slot of=k.diagrams.shape key=source many=true kind=atom type=k.diagrams.source by=name core.source="hand-core 1"

# Which knowledge of the catalog fills a kind of diagram: the facts of `type`, through its key `key` (the key that
# makes the structure: the parent, the next stage, the step after, the neighbour), each fact a node or an edge as
# `gives` says (edges: the key names the other node; order: the key is the node's place; members: the key names a
# set the node is in); `topic` the key that names what one diagram is about (the cycle, the method, the thing);
# `about` in words. `by` names the attribute of k.attributes an order fill follows when its key is a rank (the planets
# by distance from the Sun: `key=order by=distance`; by size: `key=size_rank by=size`), so that a host reading "a
# timeline of the planets by distance" takes the fill whose `by` is the request's criterion.
@k.diagrams.fill core.type of=k.diagrams.fill shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.fill.kind core.slot of=k.diagrams.fill key=kind id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string type=k.diagrams.kind by=name core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.fill.type core.slot of=k.diagrams.fill key=type id=true required=true kind=atom core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.fill.key core.slot of=k.diagrams.fill key=key id=true required=true kind=atom core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.fill.gives core.slot of=k.diagrams.fill key=gives required=true enum=edges enum=order enum=members enum=values core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.fill.topic core.slot of=k.diagrams.fill key=topic kind=atom core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.fill.about core.slot of=k.diagrams.fill key=about required=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.fill.by core.slot of=k.diagrams.fill key=by kind=atom type=k.attributes.attribute by=name core.source="hand-core 1"

# A topic a diagram can be drawn about (block 07:30 item 9): derived from the fills (tools/diagram-topics.mjs, rebuilt by
# the build), one fact per topic name and licence of the facts it is read from (a car in two licences is two facts). `name` the topic as its facts say it
# (making tea, car, planet, frog life cycle); `kind` (many) the kinds of diagram a fill draws of it; `from` (many) the
# types it is read from; `nodes` the nodes of its largest diagram (2 or more). A host loads these to know every topic
# word of the diagram knowledge (a speller's vocabulary: "tea" is not "sea") and to pick a topic for a random diagram.
@k.diagrams.topic core.type of=k.diagrams.topic shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.topic.name core.slot of=k.diagrams.topic key=name required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.topic.kind core.slot of=k.diagrams.topic key=kind many=true required=true kind=atom kind=string type=k.diagrams.kind by=name core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.topic.from core.slot of=k.diagrams.topic key=from many=true required=true kind=atom core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.diagrams.topic.nodes core.slot of=k.diagrams.topic key=nodes required=true kind=integer min=2 core.source="hand-core 1"

# Words for the world, its kinds and its keys.

# Words for each kind of diagram (the other names a request uses for it: "a hierarchy of the parts of a car" is a tree).
# w.lang.en's lexicon diagram.kind is these words and the kinds' names (tools/lang-en-diagram-frames.mjs).
